{{also|pull-out|pullout}}
==English==

===Verb===
'''[[pull]] [[out]]''' (of)

# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To [[withdraw]]; especially of [[military]] [[forces]]; to [[retreat]].
#: ''The troops '''pulled out''' of the conflict.''
# {{label|en|literally}} To use [[coitus interruptus]] as a method of [[birth control]].
#: ''With a tremendous groan, he '''pulled out''' and ejaculated all over her belly.''
# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To [[remove]] something from a container.
#: ''He '''pulled out''' his gun before she had a chance to scream.''
# {{label|en|idiomatic}} To [[maneuver]] a vehicle from the side of a road onto the [[lane]].
#: ''When joining a road, you should check for traffic before '''pulling out'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|removing something from a container}} [[whip out]]

